        {
          "id": 1285755735,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "This could be a slowdown for people with many columns. Despite the fact, that it breaks with the rest of the file style-wise and you should never use single-char counters.\n\nBut I don't see why the other issue should be one at all. I get the edge-case, but why not just circumvent the case for rowCount() <= 0 instead of doing it always? Should be faster and the rest is more stable. This seems to reduce stability in exchange for solving an issue.\n\nBtw, I am totally for finding a better solution for the above situation. I am not happy with it as well. But this change just does not work for me.",
          "author": {
