        {
          "id": 1285782032,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "You're right, should just handle the edge case with no rows with this, and I will change the style.\n\nMind taking a look at !9819 too? I'm not certain that it's the right approach, but the current approach of putting a delegate on a particular column in the view doesn't work when the view column number doesn't consistently correspond to the model's duration or time start column. I think it's easier to apply the delegate to the entire view as done there.",
